      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I rebooted my computer (after going to sleep), started steam, disabled swap and started the game.\nAt the start, it was the same RAM sinkhole, but I found a difference in behaviour: from time to time, RAM usage went down. Also I had really bad FPS hiccups in my 5 megabyte world. I was using an avatar made for older VRC. I changed to my optimized avatar, built for the beta in January, went to Japan Shrine, and stopped having FPS hiccups. I will upgrade proton now and look if I see any difference. (I was using proton 4.11 I think)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
